  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "OpenccNetLib v1.7.0\n\n            - Embedded the canonical built-in Zstandard dictionary for lazy, filesystem-independent default dictionary loading.\n            - Embedded the built-in CJK compatibility, Unicode compatibility, and DeTofu tables, removing filesystem dependencies from the default normalization and DeTofu paths.\n            - Built-in conversion, compatibility normalization, and DeToFu data are now loaded directly from assembly resources, improving deployment compatibility including Blazor WebAssembly.\n            - Migrated dictionary JSON and Zstd-JSON serialization to source-generated System.Text.Json metadata, improving trimming and NativeAOT compatibility while preserving existing dictionary formats and derived lookup metadata.\n            - Migrated dictionary CBOR serialization from PeterO.Cbor object mapping to an explicit System.Formats.Cbor reader/writer implementation, removing reflection-based object mapping and improving trimming and NativeAOT compatibility.\n            - Preserved the established CBOR wire format, including precomputed length and starter-mask metadata; existing CBOR dictionaries remain readable and newly generated dictionaries remain compatible with older PeterO.Cbor-based OpenccNetLib versions.\n            - The new CBOR loader accepts both legacy camelCase and corresponding PascalCase metadata field names and rebuilds missing derived metadata when required.\n            - Fixed built-in Zstd dictionary loading and conversion in NativeAOT applications where reflection-based System.Text.Json serialization is disabled.\n            - Removed CBOR trimming and NativeAOT analysis warnings previously caused by the reflection-capable PeterO.Cbor object-mapping implementation.\n            - Added public DictionaryLib.FromZstd(string) for loading an independent dictionary from an explicitly supplied external Zstandard file without changing the active global dictionary provider or conversion-plan cache.\n            - Retired DictionaryLib.LoadJsonCompressed(string); use the streaming DictionaryLib.FromZstd(string) loader for external Zstandard-compressed dictionaries.\n            - Added Opencc constructors accepting an explicit DictionaryMaxlength through an instance-owned conversion-plan cache.\n            - Added constructor-time frozen Opencc instances with immutable configuration and private plan caches based on DictionaryLib.Provider.\n            - Added per-instance custom dictionaries with the new Opencc(OpenccConfig, IEnumerable<CustomDictSpec>, bool, bool) constructor.\n            - Added Opencc.WithCustomDictionary() for creating a new isolated custom converter while preserving the source configuration and IDS setting.\n            - Per-instance custom dictionaries are layered on a snapshot of the currently active global dictionary provider without modifying global state.\n            - Custom converter instances remain isolated from later global provider changes and retain their custom dictionary when switching configurations.\n            - Ordinary Opencc instances continue using the shared global conversion-plan cache with no private dictionary or plan-cache allocation.\n            - Internalized ConversionPlanCache, DictRefs, and StarterUnion as implementation details and simplified conversion-plan/provider ownership.\n            - DictionaryLib.Provider remains the public built-in/default dictionary provider.\n            - Existing Opencc.UseCustomDictionary() and Opencc.UseDefaultDictionary() retain their process-wide behavior.\n            - Internalized compatibility normalization implementation types; use Opencc.NormalizeCompat, Opencc.NormalizeUnicodeCompat, and Opencc.NormalizeCompatExtended.\n            - Removed the unreleased NormalizeCompat(string, bool) overload; direct CompatIdeographs and two-argument overload consumers must migrate to the three named facade methods.\n            - Avoided parallel chunking overhead for segmented conversion when only one processor is available while preserving multicore thresholds and output behavior.\n            - Updated DeTofu table data and compacted the built-in CharactersTofu table to its three-column format.\n            - Removed redundant packaged copies of built-in resource data while retaining raw OpenCC dictionary files for DictionaryLib.FromDicts().",
